  "truth_boundary": "Actual Gaussian convolution density and globally C2 negative-log potential, for every probability input and eta>0. No Hessian curvature/covariance bounds, higher derivatives, Picard stationarity/local errors/history/expected cost, PBPS process or either complete main/composition. No finite input moments, density, or conditional-version premise. Source Section3.1 defines the unnormalized convolution exp(-V_eta)=exp(-V)*Gaussian. This theorem constructs the exact normalized density potential U_eta=-log(C_eta Z_mu). For Gibbs mu=exp(-V) volume/Z_V, U_eta=V_eta+log Z_V; formalizing that Gibbs specialization and constant-shift adapter remains separate. This normalization difference does not change derivatives, but the two chosen potentials are not asserted literally identical.",
